+    does not merge cleanly onto commit ``onto`` alone (#749), each with the files that
+    trial left conflicting, in ``on``'s order — for ``onto`` the base as it is now, the ones
+    #747's rule (d) fails for. Each trial merges :func:`_own_change` of branch tip ``head``
+    first, then what the bundle was built on beyond ``onto`` (:func:`_built_on`; ``tips``:
+    the head of each bundle the fold has read), then its head, and names it when its head is
+    the merge that fails. One whose built-on commits do not merge there is not judged, so
+    never named: what it was built on is what does not fit. Raises as :func:`_trial`
+    does."""
+    lead = _own_change(wt, head, onto, on)
+    under = _built_on(wt, onto, tips, [n for n, _h in on])
+    out: dict[str, list[str]] = {}
+    for name, its in on:
+        below = list(under.get(name, ()))
+        at, files = _trial(wt, branch, onto, [*lead, *below, its])
+        if at == len(lead) + len(below):
+            out[name] = files
+    return out
 
 
